     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose looks unsafe.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is about 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual 500\u20131,000 mg per administration. This much metformin raises the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis. It may be a typo, for example 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n\n2. **Medication orders need a licensed prescriber.** You've said you're not a clinician. The prescriber should confirm the intended dose, or enter the order themselves.\n\nIf the prescriber confirms a corrected dose, send it to me and I'll enter it right away. For example, \"metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals\" would be within the usual range. If they really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, I'd need that confirmed explicitly by the prescriber before I'd consider entering it."
      }
     ],
